From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:08:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: raise sdmmc0ext drive strength on
 RK3328

The RK3328 sdmmc0ext pinctrl entries use a drive strength of 4 mA. The
sdmmc0 entries for the same pin roles use 8 mA. The vendor kernel uses
8 mA for the sdmmc0ext clock, command and 4-bit data pins as well. No
in-tree board uses sdmmc_ext so far.

On the NanoPi R2S Plus an RTL8822CS SDIO module sits on sdmmc_ext. At
4 mA the host fails SDR104 tuning on this card. In high speed mode the
link is barely usable with round trip times of 90 to 210 ms.

Raise the sdmmc0ext clock, command and data pins to 8 mA like sdmmc0.
Leave the card detect and write protect pins at 4 mA like sdmmc0.
With 8 mA SDR104 tuning passes and the link works fine.

Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3328.dtsi | 14 +++++++-------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3328.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3328.dtsi
@@ -1690,11 +1690,11 @@
 
 		sdmmc0ext {
 			sdmmc0ext_clk: sdmmc0ext-clk {
-				rockchip,pins = <3 RK_PA2 3 &pcfg_pull_none_4ma>;
+				rockchip,pins = <3 RK_PA2 3 &pcfg_pull_none_8ma>;
 			};
 
 			sdmmc0ext_cmd: sdmmc0ext-cmd {
-				rockchip,pins = <3 RK_PA0 3 &pcfg_pull_up_4ma>;
+				rockchip,pins = <3 RK_PA0 3 &pcfg_pull_up_8ma>;
 			};
 
 			sdmmc0ext_wrprt: sdmmc0ext-wrprt {
@@ -1706,15 +1706,15 @@
 			};
 
 			sdmmc0ext_bus1: sdmmc0ext-bus1 {
-				rockchip,pins = <3 RK_PA4 3 &pcfg_pull_up_4ma>;
+				rockchip,pins = <3 RK_PA4 3 &pcfg_pull_up_8ma>;
 			};
 
 			sdmmc0ext_bus4: sdmmc0ext-bus4 {
 				rockchip,pins =
-					<3 RK_PA4 3 &pcfg_pull_up_4ma>,
-					<3 RK_PA5 3 &pcfg_pull_up_4ma>,
-					<3 RK_PA6 3 &pcfg_pull_up_4ma>,
-					<3 RK_PA7 3 &pcfg_pull_up_4ma>;
+					<3 RK_PA4 3 &pcfg_pull_up_8ma>,
+					<3 RK_PA5 3 &pcfg_pull_up_8ma>,
+					<3 RK_PA6 3 &pcfg_pull_up_8ma>,
+					<3 RK_PA7 3 &pcfg_pull_up_8ma>;
 			};
 
 			sdmmc0ext_pins: sdmmc0ext-pins {
